<description>
Expand four diagonal color markers into corner glyphs and add dashed grey sides between them.

Input structure
- The input is a background grid with exactly four foreground pixels.
- The foreground has two colors, each appearing twice, on opposite corners of one
  axis-aligned rectangle.

Rule
- Each marker becomes a centered 3x3 glyph: the center keeps its input color and
  the eight surrounding cells use the other marker color.
- In the open gap between adjacent glyphs on each rectangle side, paint grey dashes.
  A gap cell is grey when its nearest side-end distance is even.

Key insight
- The four pixels are rectangle corners; their diagonal color pairing defines the
  corner glyphs, and the sides are dashed symmetrically inward from both ends.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "four colored marker pixels at the corners of an axis-aligned rectangle, with two colors paired on opposite corners",
  "path": "from each corner marker, follow the rectangle side gap toward adjacent corner markers on the same row or column, excluding the cells occupied by the 3x3 corner glyphs",
  "trajectory": "paint grey dashes on side-gap cells whose nearest side-end distance is even",
  "transform": "replace each marker with a centered 3x3 glyph whose center keeps the marker color and whose border uses the other marker color; keep background elsewhere"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-17 rows x 14-18 cols, black background
  input:
    markers: exactly 4 non-black pixels on an otherwise black grid
    colors: exactly 2 foreground colors (not grey), each appearing twice
    layout: the 4 pixels sit at corners of an axis-aligned rectangle (2 distinct rows, 2 distinct cols)
    diagonal_pairing: same color on diagonally opposite corners (TL==BR, TR==BL, TL!=TR)
    rectangle: height 5-11, width 5-11 (measured as row/col difference)
    margin: each corner pixel >=1 cell from every grid edge (for 3x3 glyph clearance)
    gap: rectangle height and width both >=4 (so dash gap has >=2 cells)
  output:
    glyphs: each corner marker becomes a 3x3 block; center keeps marker color, 8 neighbors get the other color
    dashes: grey (5) dashed lines along each rectangle side between adjacent glyphs
    dash_rule: gap cells at positions 0..n-1; cell painted grey iff min(i, n-1-i) is even
    gap_span: horizontal gap cols [left+2, right-2], vertical gap rows [top+2, bottom-2]

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is trivially 4 pixels; no need for output-first)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [14,17], W in [14,18]
    2. Pick 2 distinct foreground colors from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9} (exclude grey=5)
    3. Pick rectangle corners top,bottom,left,right such that bottom-top in [5,11], right-left in [5,11], all corners >=1 from edges
    4. Assign color_A to TL and BR, color_B to TR and BL
    5. Place 4 pixels on black grid; this is the input
